From f80113b549a86af35485cdbb213612ebe327f7c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 09:55:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] refactor(backend): remove broken legacy api-football
 provider
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

fetch_players() was being called with football-data.org team ids — the two
providers don't share an id space, so every call 404ed. The function was the
only consumer of the legacy module and the only path that ever populated the
players table, so:

- Delete services/api_football.py entirely.
- Remove ingest_players_for_team (was defined but never invoked by any route).
- Document why player ingestion is now a no-op until a real provider mapping
  is wired up.

The 'Desfalques' UI still functions (returns an empty list cleanly).
---
